@@ -38,6 +38,8 @@ The selected value changes behavior as follows.
 - `2` — Curve/Camera Decel
 - `3` — Honda/Toyota
 For Toyota/Lexus, `3` uses stock SET/RES speed as the base control target and stock cluster set speed for display. Mode `1` also uses stock set speed; `0` and `2` retain existing Carrot speed selection. Honda mode `3` is unchanged. This setting does not switch the longitudinal controller or radar availability.
+
+Mode `0` has one exception: exact `TOYOTA_RAV4_TSS2_2022` with PCM, openpilot direct longitudinal control, and valid CAN applies observed stock speed changes or disabled-to-enabled transitions to the base target. An initially enabled sample only establishes a reference, local button or Bluetooth input takes priority in the same frame, lower lead/curve/map/camera targets remain effective, and no RES/SET CAN transmission is added.
